== 4.6 Chapter 4 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Contribution is best defined as],
  [sales less variable cost],
  [sales less fixed cost],
  [sales less total cost],
  [profit plus drawings]
)

#mcq(2, [A product sells for ₦120 and has a variable cost of ₦45. Its contribution per unit is],
  [₦120],
  [₦165],
  [₦75],
  [₦45]
)

#mcq(3, [Using the same product, the contribution-to-sales ratio is],
  [37.5%],
  [62.5%],
  [75%],
  [45%]
)

#mcq(4, [Fixed cost is ₦90,000 and contribution per unit is ₦75. Break-even units are],
  [900],
  [1,200],
  [750],
  [1,000]
)

#mcq(5, [Break-even sales value is fixed cost divided by the],
  [selling price],
  [C/S ratio],
  [contribution per unit],
  [variable cost per unit]
)

#mcq(6, [Fixed cost ₦90,000 and C/S ratio 62.5 per cent. Break-even sales value is],
  [₦90,000],
  [₦56,250],
  [₦120,000],
  [₦144,000]
)

#mcq(7, [A firm sells 2,000 units at ₦120, with variable cost ₦45 and fixed cost ₦90,000. Its profit is],
  [₦90,000],
  [₦60,000],
  [₦150,000],
  [₦240,000]
)

#mcq(8, [The margin of safety in units is],
  [budgeted sales plus break-even sales],
  [break-even sales less budgeted sales],
  [fixed cost ÷ contribution],
  [budgeted sales less break-even sales]
)

#mcq(9, [Budgeted sales 2,000 units, break-even 1,200 units. The margin of safety as a percentage is],
  [80%],
  [40%],
  [60%],
  [20%]
)

#mcq(10, [Profit can be computed as the margin of safety in units multiplied by the],
  [selling price],
  [fixed cost per unit],
  [contribution per unit],
  [variable cost per unit]
)

#mcq(11, [To find the units needed for a target profit, the target is],
  [deducted from the fixed cost],
  [ignored],
  [added to the fixed cost before dividing],
  [multiplied by the C/S ratio]
)

#mcq(12, [Fixed cost ₦90,000, contribution ₦75 a unit, target profit ₦30,000. Units required are],
  [1,600],
  [1,200],
  [1,700],
  [1,500]
)

#mcq(13, [A target profit of ₦21,000 after tax at 30 per cent requires a before-tax profit of],
  [₦21,000],
  [₦30,000],
  [₦14,700],
  [₦27,300]
)

#mcq(14, [Under marginal costing, fixed overhead is],
  [treated as a variable cost],
  [written off against the period's contribution],
  [carried forward as stock],
  [included in the product cost]
)

#mcq(15, [When production exceeds sales, absorption costing reports],
  [a lower profit than marginal costing],
  [the same profit as marginal costing],
  [a higher profit than marginal costing],
  [an operating loss]
)

#mcq(16, [The difference between the two methods' profits equals],
  [the stock movement × fixed overhead per unit],
  [the fixed cost of the period],
  [the sales × C/S ratio],
  [the contribution of the closing stock]
)

#mcq(17, [Opening stock 100 units, closing stock 400 units, fixed overhead absorbed at ₦10 a unit. Absorption profit exceeds marginal profit by],
  [₦3,000],
  [₦1,000],
  [₦5,000],
  [₦4,000]
)

#mcq(18, [A special order should be accepted at a price above variable cost only if],
  [the firm has spare capacity and the existing market is unaffected],
  [the price exceeds the normal selling price],
  [the order is large],
  [the fixed cost has been paid]
)

#mcq(19, [A sunk cost is],
  [a variable cost],
  [a cost that will be incurred in future],
  [the same as an opportunity cost],
  [a cost already incurred that cannot be changed by the decision]
)

#mcq(20, [Opportunity cost is],
  [a past cost],
  [a fixed cost],
  [the cost recorded in the ledger],
  [the cost of the next best alternative forgone]
)

#mcq(21, [When machine hours are the limiting factor, products should be ranked by],
  [contribution per machine hour],
  [profit per unit],
  [selling price],
  [contribution per unit]
)

#mcq(22, [Product A contributes ₦60 and takes 4 hours; product B contributes ₦24 and takes 1 hour. The better use of a machine hour is],
  [B, at ₦24 an hour],
  [A, at ₦15 an hour],
  [they are equal],
  [A, at ₦60 an hour]
)

#mcq(23, [Break-even analysis assumes that],
  [selling price falls as sales rise],
  [fixed cost varies with output],
  [variable cost per unit is constant],
  [there is only one product]
)

#mcq(24, [A limitation of break-even analysis is that it],
  [uses contribution],
  [can be drawn on a chart],
  [is based on cost],
  [assumes a single product or a constant sales mix]
)

#mcq(25, [The break-even chart shows the break-even point where],
  [the total-cost line crosses the vertical axis],
  [the sales line crosses the fixed-cost line],
  [the fixed-cost line crosses the horizontal axis],
  [the sales line crosses the total-cost line]
)

#mcq(26, [At the break-even point, contribution equals],
  [zero],
  [the variable cost],
  [the profit],
  [the fixed cost]
)

#mcq(27, [If the selling price rises with costs unchanged, the break-even point],
  [falls],
  [is unchanged],
  [becomes zero],
  [rises]
)

#mcq(28, [If fixed cost rises with everything else unchanged, the margin of safety],
  [becomes 100 per cent],
  [falls],
  [rises],
  [is unchanged]
)

#mcq(29, [A product has a contribution of ₦15 and sells for ₦50. Its variable cost is],
  [₦50],
  [₦65],
  [₦15],
  [₦35]
)

#mcq(30, [Sales are ₦200,000 and the C/S ratio is 40 per cent. Contribution is],
  [₦200,000],
  [₦40,000],
  [₦120,000],
  [₦80,000]
)

#mcq(31, [Using the last figures, if fixed cost is ₦60,000 the profit is],
  [₦140,000],
  [₦80,000],
  [₦60,000],
  [₦20,000]
)

#mcq(32, [Marginal costing is particularly useful for],
  [ valuing closing stock for published accounts],
  [preparing a trial balance],
  [short-term decisions such as accepting an order],
  [calculating depreciation]
)

#mcq(33, [Which cost is NOT relevant to a decision?],
  [the rent of an extra machine hired for the order],
  [the extra material needed],
  [a past cost of market research already paid],
  [the wages of extra staff]
)

#mcq(34, [A department shows a positive contribution but a loss after its share of fixed cost. In the short run the firm should],
  [close it immediately],
  [ignore its contribution],
  [raise its share of fixed cost],
  [keep it, because it contributes to the common fixed cost]
)

#mcq(35, [The C/S ratio is also known as the],
  [profit-volume ratio],
  [stock turnover ratio],
  [gross margin ratio],
  [current ratio]
)

#mcq(36, [If the C/S ratio is 25 per cent, the variable cost is],
  [75 per cent of sales],
  [100 per cent of sales],
  [25 per cent of sales],
  [50 per cent of sales]
)

#mcq(37, [A firm breaks even at ₦300,000 of sales and has a C/S ratio of 30 per cent. Its fixed cost is],
  [₦100,000],
  [₦30,000],
  [₦210,000],
  [₦90,000]
)

#mcq(38, [Absorption costing is preferred for external reporting because it],
  [matches the fixed production cost to the units that caused it],
  [shows a higher profit],
  [uses contribution],
  [avoids fixed costs altogether]
)

#mcq(39, [A firm with spare capacity receives an order at ₦40 when the normal price is ₦60 and variable cost is ₦32. The order should be],
  [accepted only if the whole fixed cost is charged to it],
  [accepted, because it adds ₦8 a unit of contribution],
  [rejected, because fixed cost is not covered],
  [rejected, because the price is below the normal price]
)

#mcq(40, [Sales are ₦500,000 and variable cost is ₦300,000. The C/S ratio is],
  [166%],
